      "source": [
        "## **PART 4 - KV Cache: Prefill vs Decode**\n",
        "\n",
        "### Context\n",
        "\n",
        "Autoregressive generation has a performance problem. At each generation step, the model runs a full forward pass over all previous tokens to compute attention. If you have generated 500 tokens, the model has effectively recomputed a large amount of work many times.\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "### Prefill Phase\n",
        "\n",
        "**Simple**\n",
        "When you send a prompt to an LLM, the model first processes the entire prompt at once. This is fast because it is one big parallel matrix operation. During this phase, the model computes and stores the Key and Value vectors for every token in the prompt.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Technical**\n",
        "In the prefill phase, the full prompt of length $n$ is processed as a single batch. For each attention layer, the model computes $K = XW^K$ and $V = XW^V$ for all $n$ positions simultaneously, then stores them in cache.\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "### Decode Phase\n",
        "\n",
        "**Simple**\n",
        "After prefill, the model generates one token at a time. For each new token, it only needs to compute Query, Key, and Value for that one new token - and then look up the cached Keys and Values from earlier tokens.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Technical**\n",
        "In the decode phase, each step processes a single new token. The new token's Key and Value vectors are computed and appended to the cache. Attention for the new token is computed against all earlier cached keys and values, rather than recomputing the full context.\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "### Why This Matters\n",
        "\n",
        "**Simple**\n",
        "Without KV cache, a 1000-token response would require the model to redo the full attention computation 1000 times, each time re-reading all previous tokens. With KV cache, each step is fast.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Technical**\n",
        "KV cache trades memory for compute. The cost of serving long-context requests is dominated by the memory footprint of the cache, not the compute. At batch_size=1 and 128K context, the KV cache can become a major memory bottleneck, which is why inference systems carefully manage cache allocation."
      ],
      "id": "dMfDbJ53R8b8"
    },
    {
